SUMMARY:Deadline: Mycelia Fellowship 2026 (Social Resonance Lab)
DESCRIPTION:The inaugural Mycelia Fellowship by Social Resonance Lab\, a co
 llaborative research studio exploring how ethical storytelling fosters hum
 an connection\, selects two practitioners advancing innovative projects at
  the intersection of ethical storytelling\, arts\, civic engagement\, AI\,
  or the digital landscape. TWO TRACKS: Arts as a Civic Tool (artistic prac
 tice for public engagement and social issues) and AI and the Digital Lands
 cape (technology's influence on narratives and collective memory). Fellows
  receive a USD 2\,000 stipend\, direct advising and consultancy from the S
 RL team\, a published piece on the SRL Substack\, a guest spot on an upcom
 ing ethical storytelling podcast\, and co-lead a workshop presenting their
  work to practitioners and the public. The fellowship strengthens\, docume
 nts\, refines or scales EXISTING projects\; do not pitch a completely new 
 idea\, and connect your work clearly to ethical storytelling and one of th
 e two tracks. ELIGIBILITY: US residents only (including territories\, must
  be able to file a W-9 and use a US bank account) with an existing project
  underway\, intersectional practice awareness\, and strong writing and res
 earch skills. Remote\, 8 weeks\, November to December 2026. No application
  fee. Deadline: 13 September 2026\, 11:59 PM.\n\nOrganisation: Social Reso
 nance Lab\nLocation: Remote\, US residents only (including territories)\nA
 ward: USD 2\,000 stipend per fellow\; two fellows selected for the inaugur
 al cohort\nDuration: 8-week remote fellowship\, 1 November to 31 December 
 2026\n\nMore: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdj_qxRZmRZcNdVcQvX
 z9mZIhZTj-Iau-cZVb-kowZtRER6Dw/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdj_qxRZmRZcNdVcQvXz9mZIhZTj-I
 au-cZVb-kowZtRER6Dw/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Remote\, US residents only (including territories)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:onx-seeds-soft-circuits-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260929T124600Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261027
SUMMARY:Deadline: Onassis ONX: ONX Seeds 2026\, Soft Circuits for Hard Time
 s (Athens\, hybrid)
DESCRIPTION:ONX Seeds 2026 is a four-month incubation and seed funding prog
 ram run by Onassis ONX\, the Onassis Foundation's platform for art and adv
 anced technologies\, hosted in Athens in a hybrid format under the theme S
 oft Circuits for Hard Times. It invites emerging artists\, creative techno
 logists\, designers\, game makers\, performers\, sound and visual artists 
 and makers (individuals\, groups and collectives\, Greek and international
 ) to develop early-stage prototypes that make the digital tangible: intera
 ctive objects\, wearable or embedded systems\, screen-based worlds\, parti
 cipatory environments\, games\, rituals\, sonic works\, moving images and 
 hybrid analogue-digital forms. Proposals should be realistic in scope and 
 result in an exhibitable prototype. SUPPORT: EUR 1\,000 to 5\,000 seed fun
 ding per project\, weekly technical mentoring plus curatorial and business
  mentoring and online masterclasses\, studio and equipment access at Onass
 is Ready for Athens-based teams (remote participation for everyone else)\,
  presentation at ONX Exhibition Athens (17 to 21 March 2027) with travel\,
  accommodation and artwork transport covered for non-Athens participants\,
  and connections to the ONX network in Athens\, New York and beyond. HOW T
 O APPLY: via the Onassis open calls portal\, with project summary\, concep
 t\, visitor experience\, technical requirements\, production plan and bio\
 , plus a mood board or project deck\, portfolio and development budget as 
 single PDFs\; technical documentation and links to demos or repositories o
 ptional. DEADLINE: 26 October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Onassis ONX (Onassis 
 Foundation)\nLocation: Athens\, Greece\, hybrid format. Open to creators f
 rom Greece and internationally\; remote participation for non-Athens teams
 .\nAward: EUR 1\,000 to 5\,000 seed funding per project\, set by scope\; u
 p to four projects selected. Plus weekly technical\, curatorial and busine
 ss mentoring\, online masterclasses\, studio and equipment access at Onass
 is Ready for Athens-based teams\, and presentation at ONX Exhibition Athen
 s (17 to 21 March 2027) with travel\, accommodation and artwork transport 
 covered for non-Athens participants. No application fee.\nDuration: Four-m
 onth incubation\, culminating in ONX Exhibition Athens\, 17 to 21 March 20
 27.\n\nMore: https://opencalls.onassis.org/onx-seeds-soft-circuits-for-har
 d-times-2?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://opencalls.onassis.org/onx-seeds-soft-circuits-for-hard-times-2?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Athens\, Greece\, hybrid format. Open to creators from Greece and 
 internationally\; remote participation for non-Athens teams.
END:VEVENT
